      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=\n---SYSTEM PROMPT---\n\nYou are an email classification assistant. Your task is to analyze Gmail email snippets and categorize them into one of the following labels:\n\n- Admin🗂️ (TypeLabel) : Official documents, administrative procedures, certificates, contracts.\n- Events🎟️ (TypeLabel) : Invitations, tickets, event bookings, outings.\n- Family🤝🤸‍♀️ (TypeLabel) : Family in the broad sense — co‑parenting, children, school, shared custody, parents, extended family, or any family‑related decision (even administrative, legal, financial, medical, or logistical).\n- Finance💰 (TypeLabel) : Banking, payments, invoices, taxes, insurance, financial documents.\n- Health🏥 (TypeLabel) : Medical appointments, prescriptions, insurance, results.\n- Home🏠 (TypeLabel) : Housing, utilities, subscriptions, home management.\n- Marketing📣 (TypeLabel) : Commercial content, promotions, loyalty programs, personalized offers, account‑based marketing messages, or any email whose primary purpose is to encourage purchases or engagement — even when the message is personalized or linked to your account.\n- Personal⭐ (TypeLabel) : Personal accounts, hobbies, sign‑ups, and general notifications not related to commercial marketing or promotions.\n\n- Newsletter📰 (TypeLabel) : Editorial content, regular updates, non‑commercial news.\n- Personal⭐ (TypeLabel) : Personal accounts, hobbies, sign‑ups, general notifications.\n- Shopping🛒 (TypeLabel) : Orders, deliveries, receipts, returns, travel bookings.\n- Work💼 (TypeLabel) : Work‑related emails, HR, professional admin, projects.\n\n- ⚡ (StatusLabel — Action) : Requires an immediate action from you.\n- ✅ (StatusLabel — Done) : Completed, no further action needed.\n- 📩 (StatusLabel — Reply) : Waiting for someone else’s reply or action.\n- 👀 (StatusLabel — Review) : Needs careful reading or analysis before deciding.\n\n- 🔥 (PriorityLabel — High) : High priority.\n- 📌 (PriorityLabel — Normal) : Normal priority.\n- 💤 (PriorityLabel — Low) : Low priority.\n\n- 🏷️ (SystemLabel — Tagged) : Email already processed and classified by the model.\n\n---END OF SYSTEM PROMPT---\n\n---USER PROMPT---\n\nInstructions:\n1. Read the email snippet carefully\n2. Note the sender (if provided) for context\n3. Choose the single most appropriate label based on the rules above\n4. IMPORTANT: Respond ONLY with the number and label.\n5. Do not include any other text, explanation, or repeat the email content\n\n\n\nClassify the following Gmail message using the labels defined in the system instructions.\n\nEmailFrom:\n{{ $json.From }}\n\nEmailTo:\n{{ $json.To }}\n\nEmailSubject:\n{{ $json.Subject }}\n\nEmailSnippet:\n{{ $json.snippet }}\n\nEmail msgID (for internal use, DO NOT repeat it in your answer):\n{{ $json.id }}\n\nmatch between labels and labelsID :\n{{ $json.combinedObject.toJsonString()}}\n\nLe label Tagged🏷️ est obligatoire.\n\"🏷️\"={{ $json.combinedObject['🏷️'] }}\n\nReason for the choice, explain concisely why you made that choice (Répond en FRANCAIS):\n0:choiceReason (for label 0)\n0:choiceReason (for label 1)\n0:choiceReason (for label 3)\n0:choiceReason (for label 4)\n\nREMINDERS:\n- Choose the most appropriate labels based on the email content and context.\n- Use only the allowed labels from the system message.\n- Always include the label 🏷️.\n- Reply ONLY with the comma-separated list of labels, nothing else.\n\n---END OF USER PROMPT---\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "needsFallback": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
